<title>PERU: Peru's August lead output fell 1.0 percent.</title>
<headline>Peru's August lead output fell 1.0 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru's lead output fell 1.0 percent to 20,974 tonnes in August, compared with the same month last year, according to preliminary figures from the Energy and Mines Ministry released Friday.</p>
<p>Production rose 8.1 percent to 164,687 tonnes in the first eight months of the year compared with the same period last year, the ministry said.</p>
<p>In 1995, lead output dipped 0.4 percent to 232,540 tonnes compared with 233,510 tonnes the previous year.</p>
<p>Peru is the world's number three lead producer. State-owned Centromin is the country's largest producer of the metal.</p>
<p>--Saul Hudson, Lima newsroom 511 221-2134</p>
</text>
